---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';

const lastUpdated = '22 August 2026';
---

<!-- Starting draft — must be reviewed by a qualified professional before the site accepts real traffic. -->
{/*
  TODO — YOU MUST FILL THESE IN YOURSELF. I have not invented any of them:
    1. Legal/business name of the operator (sole proprietor name is fine in India)
    2. A real postal address for correspondence
    3. A working contact email (set SITE.legal.privacyEmail in src/config.ts)
    4. Whether a Data Protection Officer / DPDP "Data Protection Officer" or
       "Consent Manager" is required for you — most small publishers are NOT
       Significant Data Fiduciaries under the DPDP Act and do not need one, but
       confirm this rather than assuming.
    5. Confirm the AdSense publisher ID once approved, and name it below.
    6. If you add any email newsletter provider, name it and its location here.
*/}

<PageLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description={`How ${SITE.name} handles personal data, cookies and third-party advertising.`}
  path="/privacy-policy"
  subtitle="What is collected, who collects it, and how to opt out."
  updated={lastUpdated}
>
  <p>
    This policy explains how {SITE.legal.entityName} ("we", "us") handles information
    when you visit {SITE.url}. It describes what this site actually does — not a
    generic template. The site is operated from India and is read worldwide,
    including in the EU, the UK and the United States.
  </p>

  <h2>The short version</h2>

  <ul>
    <li>There is no account system. You are never asked to identify yourself to read.</li>
    <li><strong>We set no cookies of our own.</strong></li>
    <li>We do not sell or share personal information for money.</li>
    <li>
      Our analytics is cookieless and reports only aggregate numbers — it cannot
      identify you.
    </li>
    <li>
      Advertising is served by Google and <strong>does</strong> use cookies. That part
      is described in detail below, and it is the only part that involves tracking.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What we collect ourselves</h2>

  <h3>Nothing you type, unless you send it</h3>

  <p>
    The site is a set of static files. It runs no code of its own on a server when you
    visit, and it has no database. If a newsletter signup form is active and you use
    it, the address you enter goes to our email provider and is used only to send that
    newsletter; every issue carries a one-click unsubscribe link.
  </p>

  <h3>Analytics — Cloudflare Web Analytics</h3>

  <p>
    We use Cloudflare Web Analytics to see which articles are read and how quickly
    pages load. It is <strong>cookieless</strong>: it stores nothing on your device,
    sets no identifier, and does not track you between sites or between visits. It
    reports aggregate counts — page views, referrer, country, browser family, and page
    speed measurements. We cannot single you out from it, and neither can we link it
    to anything else.
  </p>

  <h3>Hosting logs — Cloudflare Pages</h3>

  <p>
    The site is hosted on Cloudflare Pages. As part of delivering pages and protecting
    the service from abuse, Cloudflare processes standard technical information
    including your IP address, user agent, the URL requested and a timestamp. This is
    ordinary server logging performed by our host, retained by them for a limited
    period under their own policies.
  </p>

  <h2>Advertising — Google AdSense</h2>

  <p>
    This site is funded by advertising served through Google AdSense. This is the only
    part of the site that involves cookies and tracking, and it is worth reading
    carefully.
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li>
      Google and its advertising partners use cookies and similar technologies to
      serve ads, measure whether they were seen or clicked, and — depending on your
      consent and your location — to show ads based on your interests and your prior
      visits to this and other websites.
    </li>
    <li>
      Third-party vendors, including Google, use the <strong>DoubleClick</strong>
      cookie and comparable identifiers for this purpose.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>We never receive, store, or have access to the personal data these
      networks collect.</strong> We see only aggregate earnings and performance
      figures. Their handling of that data is governed by their policies, not by this
      one.
    </li>
    <li>
      If you are in the EEA, the UK or Switzerland, you will be shown a consent
      request before personalised advertising cookies are set. That request is
      operated by Google's certified Consent Management Platform. Your choice is
      recorded and you can change it at any time through the same interface.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    Full detail on how Google uses information from sites that use its services is at
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">
      policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>How to opt out of personalised ads</h2>

  <ul>
    <li>
      Turn off ad personalisation for your Google account at
      <a href="https://myadcenter.google.com/" rel="noopener">myadcenter.google.com</a>
      or <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" rel="noopener">google.com/settings/ads</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Opt out of third-party vendor cookies via
      <a href="https://optout.aboutads.info/" rel="noopener">optout.aboutads.info</a>,
      <a href="https://optout.networkadvertising.org/" rel="noopener">optout.networkadvertising.org</a>,
      or <a href="https://www.youronlinechoices.eu/" rel="noopener">youronlinechoices.eu</a> in Europe.
    </li>
    <li>If you are in the EEA or UK, revisit the consent prompt to withdraw consent.</li>
    <li>Block or delete cookies in your browser settings at any time.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    Opting out stops ads being <em>personalised</em>. It does not remove ads, and
    non-personalised ads may still use limited data for frequency capping and fraud
    prevention.
  </p>

  <h2>Local storage — your theme choice</h2>

  <p>
    The site stores two values in your browser's local storage: your light/dark mode
    preference and your chosen accent colour. These exist so the page does not flash
    the wrong colours on your next visit. They never leave your device, are not
    cookies, are never sent to us, and clearing your site data removes them.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>

  <h3>If you are in the EU or the UK (GDPR / UK GDPR)</h3>

  <p>
    Our legal bases are <strong>consent</strong> for personalised advertising cookies
    and for the newsletter, and <strong>legitimate interests</strong> for operating,
    securing and measuring the site in aggregate. You have the right to access,
    rectify, erase, restrict and object to processing, the right to data portability,
    and the right to withdraw consent at any time. You may also lodge a complaint with
    your national supervisory authority.
  </p>

  <p>
    In practice we hold almost nothing about you directly — most requests concerning
    advertising data must go to Google, since they are the party that holds it.
  </p>

  <h3>If you are in India (DPDP Act 2023)</h3>

  <p>
    Under the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 you have the right to access
    a summary of your personal data being processed, to correct or complete it, to
    erase it, to nominate another person to exercise your rights, and to a grievance
    redressal process. Where we rely on your consent, you may withdraw it as easily as
    you gave it. Send grievances to the contact address below; we will respond within
    the period the Act requires.
  </p>

  <h3>If you are in California (CCPA/CPRA)</h3>

  <p>
    You have the right to know what personal information is collected and to request
    its deletion. We do not sell personal information for money. Advertising cookies
    may constitute "sharing" for cross-context behavioural advertising; use the opt-out
    links above to stop it.
  </p>

  <h2>Retention</h2>

  <p>
    We hold no personal data ourselves other than a newsletter address, if you give
    one, which is kept until you unsubscribe. Analytics is aggregate and retains no
    identifiers. Hosting logs are retained by Cloudflare under their policy.
    Advertising data is retained by Google under theirs.
  </p>

  <h2>International transfers</h2>

  <p>
    We are based in India; our hosting, analytics and advertising providers process
    data in the United States and elsewhere. Where transfers out of the EEA or UK are
    involved, those providers rely on their own safeguards, typically Standard
    Contractual Clauses.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>

  <p>
    This site is intended for adults and is not directed at children. We do not
    knowingly collect personal data from children. Under the DPDP Act, processing
    children's data requires verifiable parental consent, which we do not seek because
    we do not target children. If you believe a child has provided information, contact
    us and we will delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>

  <p>
    We will update this page when what we do changes — in particular before adding any
    new analytics, email or advertising provider. The date at the top is the date of
    the most recent revision.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>

  <p>
    {SITE.legal.entityName}<br />
    {SITE.legal.address}<br />
    <a href={`mailto:${SITE.legal.privacyEmail}`}>{SITE.legal.privacyEmail}</a>
  </p>
</PageLayout>
